.#-----------------------------------------------------
.input|xwiki/2.1
.# Inline verbatim is rendered using the macro syntax with the reserved "verbatim" id, which keeps its content as is
.# (without any escaping, including the spaces and the empty content). A content containing a backtick that doesn't
.# start a code span (which could hide the closing tag) is rendered as a code span instead, using a backtick string that
.# doesn't appear in the content. See verbatim2.test for the parsing of the generated Markdown.
.#-----------------------------------------------------
a {{{x|y}}} b {{{**not bold**}}} c {{{a`b}}} d {{{`a``b`}}} e {{{ f }}} g {{{}}} h {{{ }}} i
.#-----------------------------------------------------
.expect|markdown/1.2
.#-----------------------------------------------------
a {{verbatim}}x|y{{/verbatim}} b {{verbatim}}**not bold**{{/verbatim}} c ``a`b`` d {{verbatim}}`a``b`{{/verbatim}} e {{verbatim}} f {{/verbatim}} g {{verbatim}}{{/verbatim}} h {{verbatim}} {{/verbatim}} i